
Complete guide: Transfer files from Windows to Ubuntu using SCP in VirtualBox
Follow these steps in order. We will configure SSH, set up VirtualBox port forwarding, test the connection, and transfer your file or folder.

What we are going to do

Check your Windows file or folder.
Start Ubuntu VirtualBox.
Install and enable SSH in Ubuntu.
Configure VirtualBox port forwarding.
Test SSH from Windows.
Transfer files using SCP.
Verify the transferred files in Ubuntu.
Step 1: Check your file in Windows
Open Windows Command Prompt (CMD).

You mentioned that your folder is located at:

D:\filetransfer

Check whether it exists:

dir D:\filetransfer
If you see your files, continue.

For example, if the folder contains file.txt, you can transfer either the individual file or the entire folder.

Step 2: Start Ubuntu in VirtualBox
