Step 3: Open Ubuntu Terminal
Linux System Cleanup Tools For Disk Space Optimization - Techy20
techy20.com
Press:

Ctrl + Alt + T

A terminal window will open.

Important: All commands in Steps 4 and 5 must be executed inside Ubuntu Terminal, not Windows CMD.

Step 4: Install SSH server
Execute:

sudo apt update
Wait for the update to finish.

Then execute:

sudo apt install openssh-server -y
Wait until installation finishes.

Step 5: Enable and start SSH
Execute these commands one by one:

Enable SSH automatically:

sudo systemctl enable ssh
Start SSH:

sudo systemctl start ssh
Check SSH status:

sudo systemctl status ssh
Expected status: Active (running)
If you see Active (running), SSH is working.

Press q to exit the status screen.

Step 6: Shut down Ubuntu
Before configuring VirtualBox:

Click the Ubuntu power menu.

Select Shut Down.

Wait until the virtual machine is completely powered off.

Do not save the VM state; shut it down completely.

Step 7: Configure VirtualBox port forwarding
