Step 8: Start Ubuntu again
Select your Ubuntu VM.

Click Start.

Log in to Ubuntu.

Open Terminal using Ctrl + Alt + T.

Check SSH:

sudo systemctl status ssh
Make sure it displays:

Active (running)

Step 9: Test SSH connection from Windows
Now go back to Windows CMD.

Execute:

ssh -p 2222 vboxuser@127.0.0.1
Here:

2222 = VirtualBox host port.

vboxuser = Your Ubuntu username.

127.0.0.1 = Your Windows local address.

If asked:

Are you sure you want to continue connecting (yes/no/[fingerprint])?
Type:

yes
Then enter your Ubuntu password.

SSH connection successful
You should now be connected to Ubuntu.

To return to Windows CMD, type:

exit
Step 10: Transfer your file from Windows to Ubuntu
You mentioned your Windows folder is:

D:\filetransfer

There are two ways to transfer.

Option A: Transfer the entire folder

Run this in Windows CMD:

scp -r -P 2222 "D:\filetransfer" vboxuser@127.0.0.1:~
Option B: Transfer only file.txt

scp -P 2222 "D:\filetransfer\file.txt" vboxuser@127.0.0.1:~
Wait until the transfer finishes.

Step 11: Verify the transferred files in Ubuntu
Open Ubuntu Terminal.

If you transferred the entire folder:

ls -l ~
You should see:

filetransfer
Check its contents:

ls -l ~/filetransfer
If you transferred only file.txt:

ls -l ~/file.txt
File transfer completed!
